#. module: import_metadata
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_import_metadata
msgid ""
"===============\n"
"Import Metadata\n"
"===============\n"
"\n"
".. \n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! This file is generated by oca-gen-addon-readme !!\n"
"   !! changes will be overwritten.                   !!\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! source digest: sha256:33f96c7b7fcf7f561dcc92eee6f576c5f58803fd482ca3267edcaf66c08c7556\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Beta-yellow.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Beta\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-LGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: LGPL-3\n"
".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-GetFluvo%2Faddons-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/GetFluvo/addons/tree/20.0/import_metadata\n"
"    :alt: GetFluvo/addons\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3|\n"
"\n"
"Import the original creation and last update user and date of records,\n"
"the ``create_uid``, ``create_date``, ``write_uid`` and ``write_date``\n"
"fields.\n"
"\n"
"Odoo always sets these fields itself, and drops any value given for\n"
"them. When data is migrated from another system, the original author and\n"
"dates are lost. With this module, an administrator can keep them by\n"
"importing with the ``write_metadata`` key in the context.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Use Cases / Context\n"
"===================\n"
"\n"
"Migrations often have to keep who created a record and when: the date a\n"
"customer was created, the author of a note, the history of a document.\n"
"Odoo does not allow setting these fields, even through an import.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Import with ``write_metadata`` in the context, as a user of the\n"
"*Administration / Settings* group, and add any of the ``create_uid``,\n"
"``create_date``, ``write_uid`` and ``write_date`` columns. For example\n"
"with ``load()`` through JSON-RPC or XML-RPC:\n"
"\n"
".. code:: python\n"
"\n"
"   models.execute_kw(\n"
"       db, uid, password, \"res.partner\", \"load\",\n"
"       [[\"name\", \"create_uid\", \"create_date\"],\n"
"        [[\"Azure Interior\", \"Marc Demo\", \"2016-01-02 03:04:05\"]]],\n"
"       {\"context\": {\"write_metadata\": True, \"tz\": \"UTC\"}},\n"
"   )\n"
"\n"
"The user columns accept what any many2one column of an import accepts:\n"
"\n"
"- ``create_uid``: the name of the user\n"
"- ``create_uid/id``: the XML ID of the user\n"
"- ``create_uid/.id``: the database id of the user\n"
"\n"
"The dates are in the ``YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`` format. Like any date of an\n"
"import, ``load()`` reads them in the timezone of the context, or else of\n"
"the importing user, and stores them in UTC. Pass ``\"tz\": \"UTC\"`` in the\n"
"context to import UTC dates unchanged. Empty cells keep the value Odoo\n"
"sets.\n"
"\n"
"The context key also works for ``create()`` and ``write()`` called\n"
"directly, with user ids or records and datetimes or strings.\n"
"\n"
"Without the context key, or for other users, the columns are ignored as\n"
"without this module, and the import does not fail.\n"
"\n"
"Known issues / Roadmap\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"- ``write_uid`` and ``write_date`` are set again by any later write to\n"
"  the record, including writes done by Odoo itself later in the same\n"
"  transaction, for instance a recomputation of a stored field. Import\n"
"  them last, or in a separate import of the same records.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/GetFluvo/addons/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/GetFluvo/addons/issues/new?body=module:%20import_metadata%0Aversion:%2020.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* Fluvo\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"- bosd\n"
"\n"
"Other credits\n"
"-------------\n"
"\n"
"Based on the idea and the ``write_metadata`` context key of the\n"
"``import_metadata`` module of\n"
"`easier_import <https://github.com/tfrancoi/easier_import>`__ by\n"
"Thibault Francois. This is a new implementation.\n"
"\n"
"Maintainers\n"
"-----------\n"
"\n"
"This module is part of the `GetFluvo/addons <https://github.com/GetFluvo/addons/tree/20.0/import_metadata>`_ project on GitHub.\n"
"\n"
"You are welcome to contribute.\n"
